Item parsing fixtures are reduced public Wynncraft API responses from
https://api.wynncraft.com/v3/item/database?fullResult (2026-09-14).
Masterwork variants use their distinct internal names while retaining
the API's actual identification ranges, base damage, requirements and
icons. Major ID descriptions are displayed; their special effects are
not simulated by the planner.

The bundled ingredient and recipe revision 54 and tome content were
compared with the current WynnBuilder datasets on 2026-09-14 and were
unchanged (current tome-loader revision 17).

Item inspection uses a compact WynnBuilder-style card with a centered
name/icon, maximum-roll identifications, powder slots, lore and rarity.
The live Wynncraft API supplies lore and trade restrictions. The card
retains scrolling for long items and the crafted/major-ID limitations.

WynnCrafter's native editor was added on 2026-09-14 after reviewing the
upstream crafter/index.html, js/crafter.js and js/craft.js. It supports
the six-slot ingredient layout, recipe types and levels, material tiers,
weapon attack speeds, ingredient effectiveness, and compatible CR codes
and links. Consumable preview includes duration, charges and basic
healing; consumables are not treated as equipment or applied to builds.
The ingredient resource retains tier and consumableIDs metadata for this
editor. Ingredient/recipe calculations and encoding use the same shared
engine as the planner. Drafts are stored separately in crafter-draft.json.

The WynnCrafter page layout was refined on 2026-09-14 to show separate
controls, recipe-effectiveness cells, a crafted-item result card and six
ingredient cards. Narrow screens stack the sections; the entire page
scrolls. Copy Hash, Copy Short and Copy Long respectively export the CR
code, recipe link and link with the six-slot ingredient list.

WynnAtlas's native item/ingredient browser was added on 2026-09-14 after
reviewing WynnBuilder's items/index.html and ingredients/index.html.
It provides name/effect search, type/profession, rarity/tier and level
filters, sorting and paged cards, using the existing Wynncraft item and
WynnBuilder ingredient sources.

The native Atlas forms were refined on 2026-09-15 with equipment icons,
profession toggles, multi-select rarity/stars and All/None controls.
Selections within a type or tier group are ORed; separate groups and
numeric/string filters are ANDed. Numeric bounds are inclusive, with
blank bounds unbounded. Identification filters use maximum rolls; absent
stats count as zero. Excluded filters reject nonzero values, including
negative values. String filters use case-insensitive substring matching.
Numeric rows can be reordered and sorted independently, in row-priority
order. Search jumps to paged result cards; Reset clears the current form.
The layout stacks on narrow screens and scrolls without hiding controls.
Legacy Atlas selections and level intervals are migrated in memory and
saved with the tab; named builds and other tool tabs remain untouched.
These are native basic search controls, not the advanced expression
language from the website.

Crafter material labels and quantities are white, with yellow tier stars
and orange brackets. Both material labels and their tier buttons share
one row; long labels scale to fit their allotted space on narrow screens.

WynnBuilder, WynnAtlas and WynnCrafter share a typed, ID-bound workspace.
The + control chooses a tool for each new tab. tool-workspace.json copies
existing builder tabs and the previous standalone crafter draft without
modifying builder-workspace.json, crafter-draft.json or named saved builds.
Each tool saves by its own stable tab ID, including during screen changes.
